ddress><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI SHINYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>LEE CHAHN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKANO MAMORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ONOSE ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YONEKURA SEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA, SHIGETAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKANO, YOSHINOBU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, SHINYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>LEE, CHAHN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKANO, MAMORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ONOSE, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YONEKURA, SEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An ink-jet recorder includes a head part for circulating ink containing a solvent and a colorant dispersed in the solvent through an ink passage, aggregating the colorant by applying a voltage to an ejecting electrode, and ejecting the colorant so as to print a character. By aggregating a predetermined colorant right before the ejection of ink, the dot gradation is controlled. Thus, an ink-jet recorder for printing characters with high definition and high reliability is realized.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce dispositif d'enregistrement par jet d'encre comprend une partie tête, destinée à faire circuler, à travers un passage à encre, une encre contenant un solvant ainsi qu'un colorant dispersé dans le solvant, à faire s'agréger le colorant par application d'une tension sur une électrode de projection, et à projeter le colorant de manière à imprimer un caractère. Le fait de faire s'agréger un colorant déterminé, juste avant la projection de l'encre, permet de régler la gradation du point.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>